notes               = "Untitled in source. The dedication به دخترم سایه ('to my daughter Sayeh') is printed in the outer margin and is not poem body — the same daughter as shadow-daughter and my-rain, whose name means shadow. The geraniums 'hear' the scent, another of the sense-crossings that run through this stretch. Tir is month 4 → +621 = 1992. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

بوی یاسِ سپید را
شمعدانی‌هایم شنیدند...
سرخ تر شدند...
یاسِ سپیدِ من... کم‌رنگم...
تیر ۱۳۷۱

===machine===

The scent of the white jasmine —
my geraniums heard it...
They went redder...
My white jasmine... and I, gone pale...
Tir 1371

===lantern===

The scent of the white jasmine —
my geraniums heard it
and went redder.
My white jasmine... and I, gone pale...

Tir 1371

